Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:54:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 345/638] extensions: retain networking-private factory with
 stubs

Stub platforms still need the common factory's ownership and destructor definitions because Chrome installs a UI delegate factory unconditionally. Keep backend operations stubbed while compiling the common factory lifecycle.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: registered native link contained only UIDelegateFactory::~UIDelegateFactory from this target

AI_LIMITATIONS: factory compile and native CEF link remain pending; no AROS network-management backend is added

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 extensions/browser/api/networking_private/BUILD.gn | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extensions/browser/api/networking_private/BUILD.gn b/extensions/browser/api/networking_private/BUILD.gn
index 9ae8caa565..c2aa60dff1 100644
--- a/extensions/browser/api/networking_private/BUILD.gn
+++ b/extensions/browser/api/networking_private/BUILD.gn
@@ -83,6 +83,10 @@ source_set("networking_private") {
     ]
   } else {
     not_needed([ "default_sources" ])
-    sources = [ "networking_private_stubs.cc" ]
+    sources = [
+      "networking_private_delegate_factory.cc",
+      "networking_private_delegate_factory.h",
+      "networking_private_stubs.cc",
+    ]
   }
 }
